title: '[SAFETY] guarantee no remote peer can reach the approval / PreToolUse path; make bus-never-RPC a hard invariant'
---
approval-* / approval-reply subcommands exist for a local PreToolUse hook flow. A remote relay peer must never be able to inject or answer an approval; that would be a critical privilege escalation. Assert and prove the approval path is local-operator-only and unreachable from any relay-delivered message. Record bus, never RPC (messages inform; the recipient decides whether to act; no feature where a message directly causes an action) as a written architecture decision because it sets the safety ceiling. Regression test: test_remote_message_cannot_reach_approval_path. Source: friction-points-cn.md.